1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
I’m Ivan. I built Readmory

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
to come back to the books and ideas I keep.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Connect your Kobo by USB
and enable its storage connection.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Choose the Kobo folder or source files,
review the preview, and save.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
This demonstration uses synthetic files.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Then let’s browse my current library.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Now here’s my cleaned current library.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
I can browse the shelf
and see each book’s cover and progress.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Let’s find Taipei Story.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
When I open it,
the reader records stay visible.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Below them are the book’s highlights and notes.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
I can scroll through the whole collection
and return to passages I want to remember.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
I can narrow the statistics
to a year and month.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The result changes,
and estimated time stays labeled.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,000
For a closer look, I’ll pick a reading day
and expand its sessions.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Now I can see the times behind it.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,000
The knowledge library brings highlights
from my books into one collection.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
I can scroll through the ideas I’ve kept,

19
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
with each passage linked to its book.

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
And when I remember a phrase,
I can search for it

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
and find the passage again.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
My own words have a separate view.

23
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
I can expand the original passage
to see what prompted a note.

24
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The library stays in this browser,
without an account.

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Cover lookup is optional.

26
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
I can download a backup
to keep a portable copy.

27
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Readmory is open source
and in public beta.

28
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Try it, and share your feedback.
